{
  "$comment": "Part X7's right-to-left styles (docs/design/output-and-languages.md §13, §21.8; step S3b). Every stylesheet of ours names sides by their logical form (margin-inline-start, inset-inline-end, text-align: start, …), which computes to the same box in a left-to-right page. 'kept' lists the rules whose physical left and right stay, each with its reason; 'ltr' the containers that keep left to right in a right-to-left page; 'rtl' the rules that apply only in a right-to-left page (:dir(rtl)), which never match in English. A kept entry with 'mirror' names the rtl rule that mirrors it. scripts/i18n/rtl-sites.mjs and test 76 fail on a physical declaration that is neither converted nor kept, a kept entry that matches nothing, a container without direction: ltr, and a :dir() rule not listed here. The other account's stylesheets (pending.json) and i18n/scripts.css (part P6's) are not read.",
  "reasons": {
    "timeline": "On the time axis inside .timeline (direction: ltr): the ruler, tracks, clips, markers, trims and playhead are placed by time from the left in every language (§13.1).",
    "transport": "In the transport (direction: ltr) with the play button, the timecode and the preview speed, which keep their order in every language (§13.1).",
    "preview": "On the preview's picture inside .canvas-wrap (direction: ltr): handles and labels placed at the frame's own coordinates (§13.1).",
    "picture": "On a picture of the video or the screen: the area picker, the guide's screenshot adjuster and the corner picker, whose positions are the picture's own.",
    "centred": "Centred with left: 50% and translateX(-50%), the same box in both directions.",
    "window": "Room for the window's own buttons, which the frame draws on the right in every language (Electron's locale stays en-US).",
    "recording": "The recording bar's countdown (Toolbar.tsx, the other account's): a window that stays English and left to right (§9.5).",
    "glyph": "Draws a play sign, a real object's shape that does not mirror (§13.2).",
    "mirrored": "A move or position with no logical form (translateX, background-position): the rule named in 'mirror' gives its right-to-left counterpart.",
    "rtl": "Applies only in a right-to-left page: the counterpart that a rule listed under 'rtl' gives (a :dir(rtl) rule, or the keyframes it names)."
  },
